@cognaiger9 I pushed `48c37082` to your branch: Enable mixed FA3/FA4 image masks and multimodal graph exclusion, and reject unsupported SM8x promotion.
Please pull before your next push. The review runs again on the new head.

<sub>Automated pre-review for `6182281c2d68`; it re-checks when the PR is updated.</sub>

@BBuf I just rebased and updated the tests.
On “image prefill after a text graph capture”: Gemma-4 cannot capture a prefill graph on main at all, regardless of attention backend. The breakable prefill graph is auto-disabled for multimodal models, and full-backend capture fails in `Gemma4TextModel.forward` with “You must specify exactly one of input_ids or inputs_embeds”, since the runner passes both for multimodal models. So there is no text graph to capture before the image prefill. The replay exclusion is covered by the existing CPU `test_fa4_multimodal_batch_cannot_replay_text_only_full_graph` for now.
I’d like to handle that in a separate PR: fix the Gemma-4 full prefill graph capture first, then add the text-capture → image-prefill case on top of this backend.

